# Bootstrap is a free, open-source front-end framework that helps developers build responsive, mobile-first websites quickly using prebuilt HTML, CSS, and JavaScript components.
 It’s widely used because it simplifies design with ready-made styles, a powerful grid system, and interactive elements like modals, carousels, and dropdowns.
# All the details about Bootstrap can be viewed in the Doc section of this link:-
https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/components/navbar/
# A CDN in Bootstrap refers to using a Content Delivery Network to quickly load Bootstrap’s CSS and JavaScript files directly from globally distributed servers,
 instead of hosting them yourself. This makes websites faster, reduces server load, and ensures users get cached versions for better performance.
# To include Bootstrap in HTML code there are 2 method:-
 1. We'll make use of the CDN and connect the code.

# There can only be 12 columns in a row. For example while creating card in a row you'll be bale to create 4 card of size 3 in one row.
# Bootstrap also has the brekpoints i.e; the sizes in which the site will be displayed in different devices.
# Container is an element in Bootstrap where the contenst will be displayed by giving equal spaces in sideways and then will be displayed.
  It will only take 100% in mobile device and in all other devices it will be in the middle by leaving spaces aside.
# Container-fluid will take 100% width in every devices.
# Grid-system
# While in full screen if you want to see the cols take full width and in mobile wants to take only 4 of them. Then you can write as follows:
 cols-12 cols-sm-4
# Inorder to specify the breakpoints you can make use of the the followong synatx for example:- cols-sm  or cols-lg  or cols-md and so on.

